==English==
[[File:Color icon yellow.svg|thumb|Various shades of yellow]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|yeallow}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}, [[yeller]] {{qualifier|dialect}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ǵʰelh₃-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|yelow|yelwe, yelou}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ġeolwe}}, oblique form of {{inh|en|ang|ġeolu}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*gelu}}, from  {{inh|en|gem-pro|*gelwaz}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*ǵʰelh₃wos}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*ǵʰelh₃-||gleam, yellow}}.

Compare {{cog|cy|gwelw||pale}}, {{cog|la|helvus||dull yellow}}, {{cog|ga|geal||white, bright}}, {{cog|it|giallo||yellow}} {{cog|lt|žalias||green}}, {{cog|grc|χλωρός||light green}}, {{cog|fa|زرد|tr=zard||yellow}}, {{cog|sa|हरि||greenish-yellow}}. Cognate with {{cog|de|gelb||yellow}}, {{cog|nl|geel||yellow}}.

The verb is from {{inh|en|ang|ġeolwian}}, from the adjective.

