===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# Having yellow as its [[color]].
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|X|line=434|text=A sweaty reaper from his tillage brought / First fruits, the green ear and the '''yellow''' sheaf.}}
#* {{RQ:Keble Christian Year|volume=II|poem=Twenty-third Sunday after Trinity|page=85|passage=Red o'er the forest glows the setting sun, / The line of '''yellow''' light dies fast away / That crown'd the eastern copse, and chill and dun / Falls on the moor the brief November day.}}
#* '''1911''', {{w|J. Milton Hayes}}, "The green eye of the little '''yellow''' god,"
#*: There's a one-eyed '''yellow''' idol / To the north of Kathmandu; / There's a little marble cross below the town; / And a brokenhearted woman / Tends the grave of 'Mad' Carew, / While the '''yellow''' god for ever gazes down.
#* '''1962''' (quoting '''c. 1398''' text), {{w|Hans Kurath}} & Sherman M. Kuhn, editors, ''{{w|Middle English Dictionary}}'', Ann Arbor, Mich.: {{w|University of Michigan Press}}, <small>[[Special:BookSources/9780472010448|ISBN 978-0-472-01044-8]]</small>, page 1242:
#*: '''dorrẹ̅''', '''dōrī''' adj. & n. {{...}} Golden or reddish-yellow {{...}} (a. 1398) *Trev. <u>Barth.</u> 59b/a: '''ȝelouȝ''' colour [of urine] {{...}} tokeneþ febleness of hete {{...}} [[dory#Adjective|dorrey]] & citrine & [[light|liȝt]] red tokeneþ mene.
#: {{ant|en|nonyellow|unyellow}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} Lacking [[courage]].
#* {{RQ:Salinger Catcher|chapter=13|passage=What you should be is not '''yellow''' at all. If you're supposed to sock somebody in the jaw, and you sort of feel like doing it, you should do it.}}
#* '''1975''', {{w|Monty Python}}, ''{{w|Monty Python and the Holy Grail}}''
#*: You '''yellow''' bastards! Come back here and take what's coming to you!
#: {{syn|en|cowardly}}
# {{lb|en|publishing|journalism}} Characterized by [[sensationalism]], [[lurid]] content, and [[doubtful]] [[accuracy]].
#* '''2004''', Doreen Carvajal, "[https://archive.is/20130629115927/www.iht.com/articles/2004/10/04/paper04_ed3__0.php Photo edict muffles gossipy press]," ''International Herald Tribune'', 4 Oct. (retrieved 29 July 2008),
#*: The denizens of the gossipy world of the pink press, purple prose and '''yellow''' tabloids are shivering over disputed photographs of Princess Caroline of Monaco.
# {{lb|en|chiefly|derogatory|offensive|ethnic slur}} Of the skin, having the colour traditionally attributed to [[Far East]] [[Asian]]s, especially Chinese.
#* {{RQ:Haggard She|passage=They were all tall and all handsome, though they varied in their degree of darkness of skin, some being as dark as Mahomed, and some as '''yellow''' as a Chinese.}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly|derogatory|offensive|ethnic slur}} Far East Asian {{gloss|relating to Asian people}}.
#* '''1913''', {{w|Sax Rohmer}}, [https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Insidious_Dr._Fu_Manchu/Chapter_2 The Insidious Dr. Fu-Manchu]
#*: Imagine that awful being, and you have a mental picture of Dr. Fu-Manchu, the '''yellow''' peril incarnate in one man.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1959|year_published=1972|author=Anthony Burgess|authorlink=Anthony Burgess|title=Beds in the East|series=The Malayan Trilogy|page=516|passage=The two youths, the brown and the '''yellow''', faced each other at the cross-roads, under a dim street-lamp.}}
# {{lb|en|dated|Australia|offensive}} Of mixed [[Aboriginal]] and [[Caucasian]] ancestry.
#* '''1938''', [[w:Xavier Herbert|Xavier Herbert]], ''[[w:Capricornia (novel)|Capricornia]]'', Chapter VI, p. 64, [https://archive.org/details/capricornianovel00herb]
#*: "Eh, Oscar—you hear about your '''yeller''' nephew?".
#*'''1965''', {{w|Mudrooroo}}, ''Wild Cat Falling'', HarperCollins 2001, p. 74:
#*:A big full-blood gin cottoned onto me. “Give us a drink, '''yeller''' feller.”
# {{lb|en|dated|US}} {{synonym of|en|high yellow}}
#* '''1933''' September 9, {{w|James Thurber}}, “My Life and Hard Times—VI. A Sequence of Servants”, in ''The New Yorker''
#*: Charley threw her over for a '''yellow''' gal named Nancy: he never forgave Vashti for the vanishing from his life of a menace that had come to mean more to him than Vashti herself.
# {{lb|en|UK politics}} Related to the [[w:Liberal Democrats|Liberal Democrats]].
#* '''2012''' March 2, Andrew Grice, "[http://www.independent.co.uk/life-style/health-and-families/health-news/yellow-rebels-take-on-clegg-over-nhs-betrayal-7469060.html '''Yellow''' rebels take on Clegg over NHS 'betrayal']", ''The Independent''
#: {{ux|en|'''yellow''' constituencies}}
# {{lb|en|politics}} Related to the {{w|Free Democratic Party (Germany)|Free Democratic Party}}; a political party in [[Germany]].
#: {{ux|en|the black-'''yellow''' coalition}}

